<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>PGP keys · bitcoin++</title>
  {{ template "rebrand_header" . }}
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/css/profile-pgp-keys.css?v=1">
</head>
<body class="btcpp-redesign btcpp-rebrand-page">
  {{ template "mainnav" . }}
  <main class="pgp-settings">
    <a class="pgp-back" href="/dashboard/profile">← profile settings</a>
    <header class="pgp-heading"><p class="whois-section-tag">§ PUBLIC IDENTITY</p><h1>Your PGP keys.</h1><p>Prove a key is yours, then share it with the community.</p></header>
    {{ if .FlashMessage }}<p class="pgp-notice" role="status">{{ .FlashMessage }}</p>{{ end }}
    {{ if .FlashError }}<p class="pgp-notice is-error" role="alert">{{ .FlashError }}</p>{{ end }}
    <section class="pgp-card">
      <h2>Add a public key</h2>
      <p>Add as many keys as you use. Each stays private until you sign a verification challenge. Your key's user IDs, including any email addresses, will become public with it.</p>
      <details><summary>Export a public key with GnuPG</summary><pre><code>gpg --armor --export YOUR_FULL_FINGERPRINT</code></pre><p>Paste the output below. Never paste a private key.</p></details>
      <form method="post" action="/dashboard/profile/keys">
        <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ .CSRF }}">
        <label for="public-key">ASCII-armored public key</label>
        <textarea id="public-key" name="public_key" rows="6" maxlength="131072" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" required placeholder="-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----"></textarea>
        <button class="pgp-button" name="action" value="add">Add key →</button>
      </form>
    </section>
    <section aria-label="Your saved keys" class="pgp-saved">
      {{ range .Keys }}
      <article class="pgp-card" id="key-{{ .Fingerprint }}">
        <div class="pgp-key-heading"><h2>PGP <code>{{ .KeyID }}</code></h2><span class="pgp-status{{ if .VerifiedAt }} is-verified{{ end }}">{{ if .VerifiedAt }}✓ Verified{{ else }}Private · unverified{{ end }}</span></div>
        <p class="pgp-fingerprint"><span>Full fingerprint</span><code>{{ .Fingerprint }}</code></p>
        {{ if .VerifiedAt }}
        <p>Signing control verified on {{ .VerifiedAt.Format "Jan 2, 2006" }}. Available publicly while the uploaded certificate is valid.</p>
        {{ else }}
        {{ if .Challenge }}
        <ol class="pgp-steps">
          <li><a href="/dashboard/profile/keys?challenge={{ .Fingerprint }}">Download your challenge</a><p>Expires {{ .ChallengeExpiresAt.UTC.Format "Jan 2, 15:04 UTC" }}. Sign the downloaded file exactly as provided.</p></li>
          <li>Sign it on your own computer:<pre><code>gpg --armor --local-user {{ .Fingerprint }} --detach-sign btcpp-pgp-challenge.txt</code></pre></li>
          <li>Open <code>btcpp-pgp-challenge.txt.asc</code> and paste its contents below.</li>
        </ol>
        <form method="post" action="/dashboard/profile/keys">
          <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ $.CSRF }}"><input type="hidden" name="fingerprint" value="{{ .Fingerprint }}">
          <label for="signature-{{ .Fingerprint }}">Detached signature</label>
          <textarea id="signature-{{ .Fingerprint }}" name="signature" rows="5" maxlength="32768" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="off" required placeholder="-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----"></textarea>
          <button class="pgp-button" name="action" value="verify">Verify & publish →</button>
        </form>
        {{ end }}
        <form method="post" action="/dashboard/profile/keys" class="pgp-inline-form">
          <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ $.CSRF }}"><input type="hidden" name="fingerprint" value="{{ .Fingerprint }}">
          <button class="pgp-button is-secondary" name="action" value="challenge">{{ if .Challenge }}Generate a new challenge{{ else }}Generate signing challenge →{{ end }}</button>
        </form>
        {{ end }}
        <form method="post" action="/dashboard/profile/keys" class="pgp-inline-form">
          <input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="{{ $.CSRF }}"><input type="hidden" name="fingerprint" value="{{ .Fingerprint }}">
          <button class="pgp-button is-remove" name="action" value="remove">Remove key</button>
        </form>
      </article>
      {{ else }}<p class="pgp-empty">No keys yet. Add your first public key above.</p>{{ end }}
    </section>
    <p class="pgp-footnote">Verification proves signing control, not a legal identity. The 16-character key ID is a short label; use the full fingerprint to identify a key. Removing a key here does not revoke it on the OpenPGP network.</p>
  </main>
  {{ template "generic_conf_footer" . }}
</body>
</html>
